# IslandView: steps from parity/shell_modules_menubar_IslandView.qml.md (batches 1-5). Screen IRICE-TEST 1920x1080 scale 1;
# the island is centred at x 960 (closed y ~14, open ~392 wide); the bar is 30 px tall.
# Each block runs in both looks: the file runs top to bottom, Material first, then Glass.

look material
setup python3 sandbox/tools/fakeplayer.py &
wait 3
shot compact
note compact pill: art, title, bars, prev/play/next (user's pieces)
ptr move 960 200
ptr glide 990 14 600
wait 0.5
shot compact-on-controls
note the island did NOT open while the pointer rests on the pill's controls
ptr click
wait 1
shot compact-paused
note the fake player paused (pill icon now play)
ptr click
wait 1
ptr glide 930 14 200
ptr click
wait 0.6
shot opened-by-click
note a click on the pill (not a button) opens the island
ipc timer toggle
ipc timer stopwatch
wait 1
ptr glide 960 700 300
wait 1
ptr move 1500 600
wait 1
ptr glide 960 14 400
wait 1
shot open-all
note music card (overlay layout: title, artist · album, seek row, transport), then rows "Focus · 24:5x left" (progress, pause+skip) and "Stopwatch" (lap+pause), then the status line
rec open 1.5 ptr glide 960 14 300
note open timing: compare with QML (first frame that moves after the 140 ms hover)
ptr glide 1137 16 300
wait 0.5
shot pin-reachable
note moving onto the pin (top right) keeps the island open
ptr click
ptr glide 960 700 300
wait 1.5
shot pinned
note pinned: still open with the pointer away
ptr glide 1137 16 300
ptr click
ptr glide 960 700 300
wait 1
shot unpinned
note unpinned: closed 260 ms after leaving
ipc timer reset
ipc timer stopwatchReset
ipc recorder screen
wait 3
shot recording
note recording pill: pulsing red dot, time, stop
ptr glide 990 14 600
ptr click
wait 2
shot recording-stopped
note one click on stop ends it; "Recording saved" alert (host/desktop recorder)

look glass
setup python3 sandbox/tools/fakeplayer.py &
wait 3
